Z||000001||MikeSchaefer||05-05-2001||07:35 PM||||Fiero Bob's show was today, and it was a ton of fun!  We met up with the Hot Rod power tour and saw a lot of great cars and great people.  Go here for a list of IL events: <A HREF="http://home.xnet.com/~nife/Events.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://home.xnet.com/~nife/Events.htm</A> <BR>Later,<BR>Mike Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||05-05-2001||08:11 PM||||It was a great day!! The Power Tour was fun. Oreif & I just got back.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/haze8588logo.gif">      </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Pennock's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A><BR><I>If you want to add your Fiero to the collection, post or send me a photo. (Sent photos ONLY to: purplehazeracing@yahoo.com )</I><P><A HREF="http://www.clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/ws6fiero" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero Club</A>||||reg||14
Z||000003||Oreif||05-05-2001||09:08 PM||||Mike, You were there? Didn't see your car.<BR>It was a great time. Got a ride in Archie's Finale too! The Power Tool was great, we saw lots of cool cars including Phil's Yellow Formula.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000004||Dave Gunsul||05-06-2001||01:07 PM||||It was a lot of fun!!<BR>Archie really went the extra mile to make people remember the Fiero.<BR>You guys should have seen Paul on the way back he lost me and me and the raffle car had<BR>to find our own way back. Didn't someone say<BR>that he didn't run his V8 hard??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>It was good to meet some of you guys that I didn't already know too.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000005||Archie||05-06-2001||04:59 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>.... Got a ride in Archie's Finale too! <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ok, Oreif, or anyone else who got a ride in my car either yesterday or 2 weeks ago at my shop, I've got a question for you.<P>Several weeks ago someone made a big deal out of telling us that the Getrag wouldn't stand up to a V-8. Now, remembering that the Finale you rode in has a Isuzu 5-speed, Do you think that the transmission can hold up to a V-8?<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||05-06-2001||09:32 PM||||There is no doubt that the Getrag or the Isuzu can hold up to a V-8. The rides Archie gave were basically 0-100mph full throttle blasts.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  (Also, his brake upgrade works very well to! Not only did it stop on a dime, but it picked it up too!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  )<P>By the way, for those of you thinking about a Finale rebody, The car looks awesome when it's coming down the road at 100mph!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000007||KissMySSFiero||05-06-2001||10:23 PM||||Archie,  <BR>you gave the term drive it like you stole it a whole new meaning.  WOW.  i went to the strip today and really discussed your swap with my uncle and i have decided if i do a swap your kits the only way to go.  i also rode in a SC3800 and it was quick.  but nothing like that good ole' yellow taxi motor you put in yours.  i cant imagine if you beefed up that motor a bit.  I'm sold.<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>     <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>      <P>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">          <BR>"When in Doubt..Whip it out!!"||||reg||1
Z||000008||MikeSchaefer||05-07-2001||02:32 AM||||Oreif, yeah I was there, I remember seeing you and I was going to say hi, but I didnt' want to brush off the old guy I was talking too.  I was in the predator kit for the tour, that car is frickin cool!  My car has some funky rmp/idle thing going on right now, so I'm not driving it.  I was VERY impressed with the work that Archie presented at the show.  Those cars can haul some serious @$$!  Has anyone noticed how popular the Fiero Bob show has become?  That had to be one of the best shows I've ever been to.  Will the power tour pass through during this same time next year?<BR>Later,<BR>Mike Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> <BR>||||reg||6
Z||000009||Archie||05-07-2001||07:40 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MikeSchaefer:<BR><B>  Will the power tour pass through during this same time next year?<BR>Later,<BR>Mike Schaefer  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hot Rod puts on the Power Tour each year but they plot a different course & schedule each time.<P>The course for next year hasn't been announced yet. Rumor says it will be from NY to San Fran.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000010||Old Lar||05-07-2001||07:55 AM||||I'll post some photos from the Fiero Bob show as soon as my computer is backup. I got back home around 10:00 last night, EST.  Its a 12.5 hour drive from Bob's.  Sunday morning he replace the starter in my 88 and readjusted the automatic shift linkage so the the over drive and drive read  on the D on the shifter plate.  A real short difference between them.  The car ran flawlessly back to NYS and I was averaging 29 mpg. At 70 mph I'm running 1750 rpm on my tach.  Bob says it will get better once the engine gets broken in.<P>The 3.4L and T440 was a great swap.  Thanks Bob.  Now to clean the four pounds of bugs off the front I picked up.||||reg||6
